    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>GMT Standard Zero</h3>
      <p>Greenwich Mean Time (UTC+0) remains unchanged throughout the year. It does not observe daylight saving, making it the global baseline clock.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>EET Standard (+2)</h3>
      <p>Eastern European Time runs at UTC+2. It is the standard winter time for Athens, Helsinki, and Bucharest, observed from October to March.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>EEST Summer Shift (+3)</h3>
      <p>From late March to late October, Eastern Europe shifts to EEST (UTC+3). During this period, the timezone gap increases to 3 hours relative to GMT.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

